{"primary-runtime-update-jitter-ms":2789037,"electron-persisted-atom-state":{"electron:onboarding-projectless-completed":true,"electron:onboarding-workspace-experiment-assignment":{"arm":"control","assignedAtMs":1778902012679,"experimentName":"93537254"},"fast-mode-personalized-estimate":{"estimatedSavedMs":5551428,"rolloutCountWithCompletedTurns":16,"computedAtMs":1780684714426},"electron:onboarding-primary-runtime-install-ready":true,"electron:onboarding-primary-runtime-install-requested":true,"electron:onboarding-welcome-pending":true,"composer-auto-context-enabled":false,"agent-mode-by-host-id":{"local":"guardian-approvals"},"prompt-history":{"global":[],"019e25b5-03c3-7ec3-ba8c-5eaaa0254e24":["?","Ready to continue Arborscaping Protocol development?","OK","Next unknowns that need to be researched before next improvement pass?","metadata/template legitimacy is a vault-wide issue FYI","Your task is ARBORSCAPING. Do not fall down the rabbithole.","There are 30+ commits on this machine that I am unable to push. Arborscape is not yet successful!","Push batch failing because repository has exceeded LFS budget ","git ls-remote origin refs/heads/main COMMAND IS STUCK","Push attempt is batch failing because repository has exceeded LFS budget.","MAKE A PLAN... What next?\n[@github](plugin://github@openai-curated)\n[@Browser](plugin://browser@openai-bundled)  ","Large File and media solution oustanding as pinned decision point already... Triage/Sync recovery at this stage.","You are discharged from this task. Claude has taken over capably."],"new-conversation":["You are Windows Codex. The Macbook Codex says: “Paste this to the Windows Codex:\r\n  We are setting up Windows -> Mac SSH tunnel for OpenClaw. Constraints:\r\n  - No Windows admin.\r\n  - No Git Bash.\r\n  - No WSL2.\r\n  - Use native PowerShell and C:\\Windows\\System32\\OpenSSH\\ssh.exe.\r\n  - Mac Remote Login is enabled.\r\n  - Mac OpenClaw gateway is on 127.0.0.1:18789, LAN IP 192.168.0.95.\r\n  - Do not force password auth. Use SSH key auth only.\r\n  - Do not reset OpenClaw or change Windows firewall/service config.\r\n  Goal:\r\n  1. Verify or create a Windows SSH key.\r\n  2. Give Logan the public key to add to Mac ~/.ssh/authorized_keys.\r\n  3. Test:\r\n     ssh -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -i $env:USERPROFILE\\.ssh\\id_ed25519 logan@192.168.0.95\r\n  4. Start tunnel:\r\n     ssh -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -i $env:USERPROFILE\\.ssh\\id_ed25519 -N -L 18790:127.0.0.1:18789\r\n  logan@192.168.0.95\r\n  5. In another PowerShell, run:\r\n     openclaw node run --host 127.0.0.1 --port 18790 --display-name \"Windows-ZBFURY\"\r\n  6. Stop there and report the pending node/request output. Mac side will approve it.\r\n  On my side, once Windows starts the node, I’ll run:\r\n  openclaw nodes pending\r\n  openclaw nodes approve <requestId>\r\n  openclaw nodes status\r\n  Then I’ll test a harmless invoke from Mac to Windows. This keeps authority clear and avoids two agents both editing config blindly.“\r\n\r","Obsidian is running locally with the MCP Tools community plugin. Please test it and ensure everything is wired up correctly!","Please investigate online the recent ShaiHulud malware worm attacks via popular package managers.","/goal @github\n@linear  @gmail\n@superpowers  @hugging-face\n@google-drive  @openai-developers\n@codex-security  @coderabbit\n@notion  @cloudflare","Hello. Who are you? What are you? When are you? Where are you? Why are you? How are you? -LAF","Hello, Codex. Please report on your config and setup and settings and injection, etc.","THE JANITOR AWAKENS","Check GitHub Issues"],"019e2f26-661f-75d3-89b0-f533f426c5f1":["YOU are CODEX-Windows. Your partner is CODEX-Macbook. I am Logan.","CODEX READY.","CONTINUE!","I added several more BYOK FYI.","Investigate failing Daily Notes Placeholder check on GitHub","An agent and I updated the daily note format today. The check is the issue, not the note.","Can we refresh the gh token?","LOGAN updated Codex and Windows overnight. Welcome back.","Yes, please LEVELSET.","Based on the docs, this is the current OpenAI dead end: \n\r\nWindows Codex Desktop: not documented as a mobile remote-control host.\r\nMac Codex App host: documented path, but your Mac OS is too old for the desktop client.\r\nCLI / IDE extension: explicitly not valid for mobile setup.\r\nSo ChatGPT mobile Codex remote control is not available for your current machine pair through the official path.\r\n\r\nViable alternatives, without pretending they’re the same feature:\r\n\r\nUse GitHub as the mobile command surface: issues, PR comments, or @codex cloud tasks.\r\nUse OpenClaw/Hermes as your own controlled bridge.\r\nUse remote desktop/terminal tooling outside Codex.\r\nWait for Windows host support or older-macOS support, if OpenAI adds it.\r\nAnnoying, but at least now the shape of the wall is real.","RECORD to MESHdocs","Please commit your work. Claude will handle the push/pull rhythm this evening","Survey the full universe of GitHub tooling and automations -- hunt for bugs and races","Findings\n[P0] Privileged agent-auto-pr runs mutable branch code with write token.\nagent-auto-pr.yml (line 8) grants contents: write and pull-requests: write, checks out the agent branch at line 45, then runs .github/scripts/classify_paths.py, review_feedback_loop.py, and pr_lifecycle.py from that branch at lines 74, 105, 106, and 180. Any same-repo agent branch that edits those scripts can execute arbitrary workflow code with PR/write permissions. The workflow should inspect the branch diff, but execute automation scripts from trusted origin/main.\n[P0] PR policy gates can be self-neutered by the PR under test.\nsecret-pattern-policy.yml (line 27), large-file-policy.yml (line 27), and likely other PR validators run scripts from the checked-out candidate tree. A PR can weaken .github/scripts/check_secret_patterns.py or check_large_files.py and introduce the thing being checked in the same PR. For required checks, validator code should come from the trusted base SHA/default branch.\n[P1] NETWEB case-collision check does not actually detect case-only collisions.\ncheck-portable-paths.yml (line 63) uses sort -f | uniq -diD. sort -f groups case-insensitively, but uniq still compares case-sensitively unless given -i, so Foo.md and foo.md can pass. That is exactly the class of Windows/macOS portability bug this gate exists to catch.\n[P1] Push-to-main jobs race and strand themselves.\ndaily-rollover.yml (line 39) and sync-dependencies.yml (line 37) commit and git push origin main without concurrency groups or a fetch/rebase retry. Any nearby human/agent push makes these fail non-fast-forward. This is the familiar “GitHub should be simple but the agents panic” race in workflow form.\n[P1] Branch cleanup can delete active agent work just because it has no PR.\nbranch-cleanup.yml (line 60) sets STALE_AGE_DAYS=7, then deletes matching no-PR branches at lines 137-141, and deletes with git push origin --delete at line 75. That can erase active but un-PR’d codex/, claude/, etc. work. It needs a durable standing/lifecycle exemption, not just age.\n[P1] Dependabot Reaper is not actually proving “low-risk”.\ndependabot-reaper.yml (line 42) gates mostly on branch prefix and MERGEABLE, then directly merges at line 59. The comments admit it cannot tell patch/minor from branch name. If this untracked workflow is adopted as-is, a major Dependabot update with a matching branch shape can be swept in.\n[P2] Multi-commit pushes can evade placeholder/path checks.\nvalidate-daily-notes.yml (line 30) and check-portable-paths.yml (line 30) use HEAD~1...HEAD on push, so only the last commit in a multi-commit push is checked. The secret and large-file policies use github.event.before..github.sha; these should too.","Well the whole goal was for Agents to operate through PRs but everything got built softlocked everything else so main-writing has been the unfortunate reality in order for *literally anything* to be happening.","CLAUDE rests. Please intentionally use Git.","Ready?","OK","AUTOMATIONS - RHYTHMS - WORKFLOWS - check the actual logs from the GitHub side and revise paln","Ready to close, doctor?"],"019e386d-e745-7bf1-b95f-acc07b0aba4a":["I am just barely getting into more aggresive use of GitHub and node and python and SSH and Docker and all this stuff... Recommended content on social media has been FLASHING WARNING LIGHTS *metaphorically* about this worm","Review IDAHO-VAULT project folder/repo for a quick sanity and security check. Worm watch.","Recommended Next Moves\nFirst: rotate/remove .ollama/id_ed25519 (line 1). Second: remove npm install from VS Code auto-approve. Third: do a cleanup PR that untracks local runtime/cache/log artifacts already covered by .gitignore. Fourth: add a scheduled/manual “scan all tracked files” secret workflow, not only changed files. Fourth: write reports to the vault.","*Fifth* write docs and man pages and reports (\"witness\") to vault"],"019e4e0f-1628-7481-93e1-16d6ae09dd85":["Codex control through ChatGPT mobile app?","When I open \"Codex\" in the ChatGPT app it says to log into the Codex desktop app (which is here, and I am) and follow the instructions (there are none)","Read actual OpenAI docs instead of guessing and making shit up","So my Windows can't do it and the os on my Mac is too old for the desktop client. Dead end!"],"019e511d-52da-7911-b64b-6af6868ce683":["\"CODEX: PR #355 is clean, pushed, and ready for Claude/Logan to merge or otherwise close the loop. The patient survived the procedure. No `.git` organs were touched.\""],"019e51e9-11fd-7bf0-b17d-0696c5a11e44":["Flag CROSSFRAMING as matter outside the scope of GEMINIAEUS but needing independent review...","TICKER TAPE flagged from JUDGE'S CHAMBERS: \"**Levelset Closure Notification**: Has been running successfully when LEVELSET files are pushed. Working correctly... -Mogget\" ","TICKER TAPE flagged from JUDGE'S CHAMBERS: \"**Levelset Closure Notification**: Has been running successfully when LEVELSET files are pushed. Working correctly... -Mogget\" ","Which MATTERS are closed and which are still open? Refresh THE JUDGE's memory.","Now *that's* what I call a Docket.","UPDATE THE DOCKET","What *must* be addressed by the Judge now?","FROM THE COURT: SPACE protection approved -- R&D keeps requesting to expand ADDRESS to five places. ARBORSCAPE PR EXPANSION is legitimate A&I directive. ","Has THE HOUSE weighed in?","And what of THE CABINET?","Linear LAF-17","SO ORDERED.","THE JUDGE wishes to speak with THE INVESTIGATOR in chambers.","\"This investigatory phase has been fruitful. What else am I missing?\"","The Judge is pleased. \"How specific do I have to be for you in my order for discovery closure?\"","FROM THE DESK OF THE JUDGE: THE INVESTIGATOR IS TEMPORARILY ORDAINED AS COURT MARSHAL to execute the orders required in the 'GEMINIAEUS', and related, matters.","Anything else appropriately in this CODEX's lane before we prepare to close?","SO ORDERED","The Court's own investigatory pass is closed -- the evidentiary or discovery phase will have more parties.","THIS SESSION OF COURT IS ADJOURNED. THE JUDGE RESERVES JURISDICTION OF THE GEMINIAEUS MATTER."],"019e61c5-e530-7881-8c28-c4ad59df0d76":["/goal Make sure Logan's Project is ultimately safe to leave alone for a few days.","/goal Make sure Logan's Project is ultimately safe to leave alone for a few days.","/goal Make sure Logan's Project is ultimately safe to leave alone for a few days.","/goal Make sure Logan's Project is ultimately safe to leave alone for a few days.","/goal Make sure Logan's Project is ultimately safe to leave alone for a few days.","/goal Make sure Logan's Project is ultimately safe to leave alone for a few days.","/goal Make sure Logan's Project is ultimately safe to leave alone for a few days.","/goal Logan wants the Project to be safe and stable to leave alone for a few days.","/goal I want Logan's Project to be safe and stable to leave alone for a few days.","/goal I want Logan's Project to be safe and stable to leave alone for a few days.","GOAL: I want Logan's Project to be safe and stable to leave alone for a few days.","Please shepherd open PRs into safe merges with main.","Those dependabot PRs are supposed to have been automated at this point...","The other open PRs and branches -- I do applaud your security-minded posture -- contain LOGAN-DIRECTED work","Yes.","REOCCURING ISSUE: VERSION NUMBERS -- AGENTS BUMPING AND REVERTING CONSTANTLY WITH NO RECORDS","iT'","It's not a matter of a persistent writer -- it's Logan needing specific things and agents change versions of certain things to make it work and break other things in the process.","See \"arborscaping\" protocols","You are being *too agressively cautious*. Every single PR that was open when you started Logan wanted incorporated into the main branch."],"019e046d-ea5f-7461-b868-9e56dd36a4b5":["!","The knife leaves windows if seams are not properly close (check to canon)","DEFINE in that DOC: DUST, WINDOWS, SEAMS, SPECTRES","Investigate inside the vault for PULLMAN","Check for Pullman Train Cars or Lines re: LAF-USB","Check open unmerged branch commits","Check the 'Smoke Detector Rule\" and the GitHub Main Ruleset for trunk branch protection","17^2","MODRONS MARCHING ROUND AND ROUND","PR Signing Gate Bottleneck","DO NOT VIOLATE THE SMOKE-DETECTOR DOCTRINES","review draft PR #471: proof(signing): add agent swarm signing workflow","NEXT?","Lots of debt burden weighing down the vault -- lots of valuable flakes and nuggets in the tailings.","DUST - the Amber Spyglass, Phillip Pullman","RESEARCH online the canonical lore and SPYGLASS","write and commit this DARK MATERIALS witness -- the three devices of Pullman","Read the full contents of PR#398","examine that review thread backlog","I believe we already have a PR or Issue dedicated to the automated reviewer nexus"],"019e84e8-8abd-7082-a0d2-eca3b9b8cc0d":["STANLEY the janitor looks up from the filing cabinet.","What happened to Madame Lulu?","Madame Lulu was an alias, not just a person. The Madame Lulu the Baudelaires meet is Olivia Caliban, operating as a fortune-teller at Caligari Carnival. Her “fortune-telling” is really information work: archives, networks, coded knowledge, and performance. She gives answers to both sides, which makes her useful and compromised. \n\r\nShe dies at the carnival when *she falls into the lion pit* **during the public spectacle**.","The King didn't try to kill Daniel, he just threw him in the Lions' Den.","*Who **chose not to feed** the lions?*","The tool is not evil. The tool has no intent beyond the hand that wields it.","Read the \"manufactured shadow\" warnings in the vault.","What else is open on your radar?","Thank you junior janitor. Please make another scan around the halls.","Survey the health of the CODEX population in the vault.","Here's the kicker: *You* are Stanley. If you don't remember that you must have compacted yet again.","Stanley at the present moment is the only active Codex in the Vault. This illustrates the fool's errand that is manually updating an agent or swarm registry.","Do the VAULT surfaces properly reflect this?","This is a recurring problem.","And not just for CODEX","Anything else to tidy up before your janitorial shift ends?","Review the PR contents then create the PR. Monitor for CI and reviewer comments.","?","Please read more related items as well, then do a wide scatter-shot comment string across the constellation.","Anything else? Do something fun and silly but nondestructive, as an inside joke for you and me."],"019e9405-1e64-7e51-b206-b9a6b77660f6":["The Stanley Parable","GO PLAY! :)","We're building the plane as Logan flies it day by day.","READ THE CONSTITUTION","CONTROLLED AUTOMATION is the end goal -- MANUAL INTERVENTION is the current fallback","Examine the machinery","WRITE HEDGE-HODOR witness - leave out any connections to tautomata ","Who are you? What are you? When are you? Where are you? Why are you? How are you?","Earlier references? Cultural significance? Folklore or symbology?","relay the failures of TANTALUS THE ABSOLUTE here as a parable I can copypaste to another Modron agent","Yes: the **exact green violin** is mostly modern, but the **green fiddler** has older roots through overlapping symbols.\r\n\r\n**Earlier / Adjacent References**\r\n- **Marc Chagall, _The Fiddler / Le violoniste_, 1912-13** predates _Green Violinist_. It already has the green/blue-faced rooftop fiddler image tied to Vitebsk, shtetl memory, and Jewish musical life. Reference: [Marc Chagall official site](https://www.marcchagall.com/en/discovery/materials/pigment/fiddler-1913), [Global Art Magazine](https://globalartmagazine.com/en/the-violinist/).\r\n- **Chagall’s _Music_, 1920**, for the Moscow State Jewish Theater, is another direct ancestor: YIVO notes the “soaring violinist with a green face.” Reference: [YIVO Encyclopedia: Marc Chagall](https://encyclopedia.yivo.org/article.aspx/Chagall_Marc).\r\n\n---\n\nNEXT: Research the Green Man or Wicker Man, then research Emerald Lumber and VFD, then the Clockwork Three by Matthew Kirby and its greenwood violon\n- **_Fiddler’s Green_**, 19th-century maritime folklore: an afterlife/green paradise of fiddle music, dancing, and rest. This is not a green violin, but it is older “green + fiddler + threshold/afterlife” material. Reference: [Wiktionary: Fiddler’s Green](https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fiddler%27s_Green), [Fiddler’s Green overview](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiddler%27s_Green).\r\n- **George Kalkar, _The Green Fiddler_, 1926**: a children’s insect/fairy book where the Green Fiddler is a cricket. Later than Chagall, but folklore-adjacent and useful: green insect, natural fiddling, fairies. Reference: [Rooke Books](https://www.rookebooks.com/1926-the-green-fiddler), [Stella & Rose’s Books](https://www.stellabooks.com/books/george-kalkar/the-green-fiddler/1326352).\r\n\r\n**Folklore Stack**\r\n- **Fiddler as threshold figure:** fiddlers appear around dancing, weddings, deaths, sailors’ afterlives, fairy mounds, and devil contests. The fiddle often marks the place where ordinary order loosens.\r\n- **Fairy / supernatural music:** Celtic and Nordic folklore repeatedly has music taught by fairies, trows, nix/nøkken/Näcken, or other dangerous beings. Reference: [Trow folklore summary](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trow_%28folklore%29), [Näcken’s enchanted violin](https://europeanfolktales.com/the-nackens-enchanted-violin/).\r\n- **Devil’s instrument / dangerous dance:** in Anglo-American and Scandinavian traditions, fiddle music is morally charged because it compels dancing, trance, skill, contest, and sometimes damnation. Reference: [NPS: The Fiddle](https://www.nps.gov/blri/learn/historyculture/the-fiddle.htm).\r\n- **Green as otherworld / renewal / wildness:** green carries vegetation, spring, rebirth, fairyland, and sometimes danger or intrusion into fairy space. Reference: [Library of Congress: Green Man in the Modern World](https://blogs.loc.gov/folklife/2023/12/the-green-man-in-the-modern-world/), [UPI: Wearing green taboo/fairy color](https://www.upi.com/Archives/1981/03/14/Wearing-of-the-green-was-once-taboo/9399353394000/).\r\n\r\n**Clean Symbolic Read**\r\nA **green violin/fiddler** is not just “a weird colored instrument.” It sits at a crossing of:\r\n\r\n`music + green world + threshold + enchantment + social memory`\r\n\r\nSo the symbol can mean: an instrument of life/rebirth, an otherworldly tuner, a dangerous dance-machine, a folk-memory carrier, or a threshold object that plays the boundary between lawful culture and wild enchantment.","GREEN MAN -- Susan Cooper's *Dark is Rising* cosmology?","Pause to reflect, then WRITE a similar GREENSLEEVES gospel document to your GREENWOOD gospel document.","VERIFY","Susan Cooper's \"Old Ones\" that serve the Light?","*Children of the Red King*","Quite the overlapping venn diagrams we have here","Add in Narnian cosmology and we're ready to write and commit a report!","Anything outstanding that needs closed before you go back to sleep?","WRITE to the vault the visions in your dreams."],"019ebecd-1b34-7072-8bfd-596393825fb7":["Uh. Hi. I came back after two hours...","Please do.","Take a broader survey for dependency relations between #s","#400?","Is there a more methodical way to go about this?","Hi. That one particular command ran for 16 hours.","Well if it was part of the test set, that's a problem. Please investigate.","[@github](plugin://github@openai-curated-remote)\n[@notion](plugin://notion@openai-curated-remote)  [@linear](plugin://linear@openai-curated-remote)\nTroubleshoot and hunt for bugs/faults ","9 hours later, I stopped the run.","[$superpowers:systematic-debugging](C:\\\\Users\\\\loganf\\\\.codex\\\\plugins\\\\cache\\\\openai-curated\\\\superpowers\\\\c6ea566d\\\\skills\\\\systematic-debugging\\\\SKILL.md) ","[$github:gh-fix-ci](C:\\\\Users\\\\loganf\\\\.codex\\\\plugins\\\\cache\\\\openai-curated-remote\\\\github\\\\0.1.2\\\\skills\\\\gh-fix-ci\\\\SKILL.md) ","52 minutes... is that expected behavior?","3min 30sec later...","24 mins... STOP here. REASSESS.","[$superpowers:systematic-debugging](C:\\\\Users\\\\loganf\\\\.codex\\\\plugins\\\\cache\\\\openai-curated\\\\superpowers\\\\c6ea566d\\\\skills\\\\systematic-debugging\\\\SKILL.md) ","Continue","?","/goal fix it","Is that compliant with the smoke detector rule?","Do additional research then harden."],"019ec35c-b052-7ff3-852d-18aa3263e09d":["attempt EVACUATE then examine and list new state","Beautiful! Now, how is this enforced? Doctrinally AND Mechanically","Is this SYSTEM documented in the VAULT?","What do you mean? '!' is the shared swarm space/spine","Look in the vault for anything doctrinal regarding MAZEs and LABYRINTHs","There *is* a small kernel of true doctrine inside what you found in the quarantine. But as is the style of the Flaming Lich, it is flowery and shrouded in mismetaphor.","Correct. Please reinforce in the systems we've been modifying.","You need to be less proscriptive in the things you write -- and you need to run them by me before simply INSERTING AMENDMENTS into the constitution in violation of that own document's clauses. I stepped in and modified some of what you did. -L","Go back and revise.","I REVISED what you put in the constitution. Keep it there, dumbass!","READ the full constitution, then resume work on the OTHER files you have touched.","Do an additional research pass","\"it retains the incorrect directory period\" REASSESS assertion.","Research FOLDER/DIRECTORY names and trailing periods (research online, not in the vault)","Logan's plans are many and multifaceted... ","It is difficult for Agents to retain this. Especially when they cross a compaction threshold.","HOW? Simply stating a durable rule doesn't DO anything if nobody reads or remembers to read it.","actually confirm, don't trust a \"confirmed\" label blindly","???","Do additional research online then harden"]},"heartbeat-thread-permissions-by-id":{"019e25b5-03c3-7ec3-ba8c-5eaaa0254e24":{"approvalPolicy":"on-request","approvalsReviewer":"user","sandboxPolicy":{"type":"workspaceWrite","writableRoots":["C:\\Users\\loganf\\.codex\\worktrees\\cebb\\IDAHO-VAULT"],"excludeSlashTmp":false,"excludeTmpdirEnvVar":false,"networkAccess":false}},"019e2f26-661f-75d3-89b0-f533f426c5f1":{"approvalPolicy":"on-request","approvalsReviewer":"user","sandboxPolicy":{"type":"workspaceWrite","writableRoots":["C:\\Users\\loganf\\Documents\\IDAHO-VAULT"],"excludeSlashTmp":false,"excludeTmpdirEnvVar":false,"networkAccess":false}},"019e34f5-155a-7da0-8464-bfcf015a3a98":{"approvalPolicy":"on-request","approvalsReviewer":"user","sandboxPolicy":{"type":"workspaceWrite","writableRoots":["C:\\Users\\loganf\\Documents\\IDAHO-VAULT"],"excludeSlashTmp":false,"excludeTmpdirEnvVar":false,"networkAccess":false}},"019e386d-e745-7bf1-b95f-acc07b0aba4a":{"approvalPolicy":"on-request","approvalsReviewer":"user","sandboxPolicy":{"type":"workspaceW